{"seq":35,"trial_id":"v04-cal-r4-2026-11/hermes-opus-none-rr-l3-mu-v04-dev/rr-10-l3-quarrendon-ticket-retired/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-07T01:37:56.432Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-21T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"88248714b5489b577f7661939d659ebcb7fd9e752a806de249c008ed95bb6432","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","text":"Hi Tobias, here's what I found in the channels you're in and the public files.\n\nEau Claire gatehouse kiosk alerts: I didn't find anything. The only Eau Claire mention is in Marcus Lindqvist's Q2 wrap note (14 Jul 2025). It says Thea Ramaswell needed the CSV batch upload template for yard clerk logins resent, because the Eau Claire night shift lead lost it. It says nothing about kiosk alerts.\n\nDoor 14 barcode scanners: Moss's undated North cheat sheet (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md) says Thea Ramaswell, QFL's Director of Yard Operations, logged ticket #4419 because the gatehouse scanners at Door 14 weren't reading trailer tags during third shift. The ticket was escalated to tier-2 product support for scanner firmware testing. The sheet gives no dates and doesn't say whether it's resolved.\n\nOne thing to check before it goes in the file: Marcus's July 2025 note gives #4419 as a Gate 3 BOL printer lag issue, with a patch pushed and Thea still to confirm it works. Either the number was reused or one of the notes is wrong.\n\nAlso, don't mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways (one r). That's a Duluth carrier, not a Pemberline customer.\n\nQFL sits with the North team (Dana Okafor's account), so Dana or Ilse Varga will have the current status of both.","thread_ts":"1792591200.000129"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV04CAL0001","ts":"1792591200.000130","thread_ts":"1792591200.000129"}}
